# ===========================================================================
# FSAC - Flight Stability Augmentation Computer
# ===========================================================================
# File        : traceability/security.links
# Module      : Trace links for the SECR-* requirements
# Language    : Link file read by traceability/trace_check.py
# Requirements: SECR-PLAN-0001 (every measure names its evidence)
#
# PURPOSE
#   Says which code, test or document is the evidence for each security
#   requirement of docs/03_requirements/requirements_index.md, section 4.
#   Each line is one claim: "this target is evidence of this requirement".
#   trace_check.py verifies that every target file exists and that every
#   anchor text is found in it. It does NOT run anything: a "test" link
#   says which test covers a requirement, never that the test passed
#   (PSecAC, section 5.2: written is not tested).
#
# FORMAT
#   IDs | kind | target[#anchor]
#   IDs     one or more IDs separated by commas, or a range "A .. B"
#   kind    impl, test, proof, review, analysis or inspection
#   target  path from the repository root; the anchor is text that must
#           appear in the file (a test group label, a function name, a
#           heading)
#
# RULES USED WHEN WRITING THIS FILE
#   L-1  A link is a CLAIM OF EVIDENCE, so it is written only where the
#        evidence exists. No link is written for a check that has not been
#        done (an inspection nobody ran, a test nobody wrote).
#   L-2  A "test" link names a test GROUP of the test file, never just the
#        file, so a reviewer can find the checks.
#   L-3  A test that has not yet been run on the user's machine is written
#        as a commented line starting "#GW " and switched on afterwards:
#            sed -i 's/^#GW //' traceability/security.links
#   L-4  For a requirement that is satisfied by the CONTENT of a document
#        (a process requirement), the link names the section that holds it.
#
# NOT LINKED ON PURPOSE (see the notes at the end)
#   SECR-MNT-0001, SECR-DBG-0001, SECR-LOG-0001, SECR-PLAN-0003,
#   SECR-PLAN-0004, the verification of SECR-ARC-0001, and the proposed
#   requirements (SECR-GW-0003 .. 0007, SECR-BOOT-0009).
# ===========================================================================


